Z||000010||Patrick's Dad||03-01-2001||02:59 PM||||There is a theory which states that if anyone ever found out why the Universe was created and what it is here for, it will immediately disappear and be replaced by something even more bizarre and inexplicable. There is another theory which states that this has already happened.<P>That was as close to a direct quote from "The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy" as I can remember, as my hardbound is still packed away (We've lived in this house for 17 months, already!), and my paperback doesn't contain this. Maybe it's from "The Restaraunt at the End of the Universe...." No Babelfish needed.<P>As (apparently) one of the more conservative members of this board (and, from the Northeast, yet), I would also like to express my respect for those of differing opinions, and would defend anyone's right to their opinion. Article One of the Bill of Rights guarantees freedom of speech (and thought) to us all, not to those who agree (or disagree) with me. I will stand next to any of you in defense of these principles.<P>Having been raised up in the (orthodox) Jewish religion, I learned a lot of lessons about "our" message vs. "your" message. I was surrounded by Irish Catholics and a Protestant. Now, technically, I am a Protestant, and I'm married to an Irish Catholic.<P>No one has yet pointed to the good done in the name of "religion," what people like to call service to God and/or Jesus. The Christian Children's fund, hundreds of years of music, even the Constitution and the foundations of American Government are drawn from a single verse in the Bible, describing God as Lawmaker (Congress), Judge (The Courts) and Ruler (Executive). As I had posted on "C vs E," my God is big enough to have made everything out of nothing, even to draw radiation (Light, Gamma Rays, etc.) from galaxies over twenty billion light years away (Which would predate the universe, according to scientists.). My faith isn't blind. It renews each time I look at my children, each time I look upon the sky with my 5" telescope and see what He painted, and so much more. Without Him, we would rely on Entropy.<P>Some of you may value this at less than $.01, some, $1.00. I'll still call you friends, though I have never met you.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/StarHeroSig.jpg"> ||||reg||2
Z||000011||Standard||03-01-2001||11:28 PM||||I think I've found more truth in <I>The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy</I> then I have anywhere else  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I have the whole 5 book trilogy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Gettin' time to read it again, too.<P>Patrick's Dad, here's the exact quote for the theory.  It is from <I>The Restaraunt at the End of the Universe</I><P>"There is a theory which states that if ever anyone discovers exactly what the Universe is for and why it is here, it will instantly disappear and be replaced by something even more bizarre and inexplicable.<P>There is another which states that this has already happened."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I love this book<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierospeeder||03-01-2001||11:45 PM||||Were the beatles GOD?? oh ya they were just more popular.<P>Im suppose to be catholic, which is how i was raised and still is.  I dont go to church because that is when all the kewl car shows are on TNN.<P>I have my own beliefs and i corporate GOD and science together.  <P>God created the big bang theorem.  And planned out that we were going to evolve from singled cell organisms.  Or was that bacteria??   And we evolved from the monkey which turned to be cavemen etc... aka Lucy found few thousand years ago.   Its that evolution thing you learn in class...<P>Sometimes i think its better that God doesn't appear in the real world because we are already living a life behind science.  Plus, if God did appear, would the world go insanse?  Just a theory of mine.  <BR>Didn't Jesus die when he appeared on earth or will we be smarter this time??<P>Religious is a scary thing to me in a way.  What scares me is to see how some people worship something that isn't there.  Like watching people go to healers on TV and all those stupid things on TV where they collect money.  And its those indiana Jones movies, but they are so kewl.    Its the thing people do for religion.<P>I thank God for creating us to make the Fiero.   It was his only reason to make us and aftermarket parts.<BR>||||reg||1
